   MMaaccrroo ppaacckkaaggee
       New manual pages should be marked up using the  ggrrooffff  aann..ttmmaacc  package
       described  in  mmaann(7).  This choice is mainly for consistency: the vast
       majority of existing Linux manual  pages  are  marked  up  using  these
       macros.

   CCoonnvveennttiioonnss ffoorr ssoouurrccee ffiillee llaayyoouutt
       Please  limit  source code line length to no more than about 75 charac‐
       ters wherever possible.  This helps avoid line‐wrapping  in  some  mail
       clients when patches are submitted inline.

